Question 6 — Calculate total marks and percentage using data binding
This question uses [(ngModel)], so we must import FormsModule.
File 1: src/app/app.ts
import { Component } from '@angular/core';
import { FormsModule } from '@angular/forms';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  standalone: true,
  imports: [FormsModule],
  templateUrl: './app.html'
})
export class App {
  m1 = 0;
  m2 = 0;
  m3 = 0;
  total = 0;
  percentage = 0;

  calculate() {
    this.total =
      Number(this.m1) +
      Number(this.m2) +
      Number(this.m3);

    this.percentage = (this.total / 300) * 100;
  }
}



File 2: src/app/app.html
<h1>Student Marks Calculator</h1>

<label>Subject 1:</label>
<input type="number" [(ngModel)]="m1">
<br><br>

<label>Subject 2:</label>
<input type="number" [(ngModel)]="m2">
<br><br>

<label>Subject 3:</label>
<input type="number" [(ngModel)]="m3">
<br><br>

<button (click)="calculate()">Calculate</button>

<h3>Total Marks: {{ total }} / 300</h3>
<h3>Percentage: {{ percentage }}%</h3>



Output example: If you enter 80, 70 and 90, the total is 240 and the percentage is 80%.

